# Supply-chain cooldown: refuse any version published less than 7 days ago.
# Hijacked-publish attacks (e.g. the March 2026 axios compromise) are almost
# always caught and unpublished within hours, so a cooldown means we are never
# the ones who install a malicious release first. Requires npm >= 11.10.0.
#
# This applies when resolving new versions (`npm install`, `npm update`).
# `npm ci` is unaffected — it installs exactly what package-lock.json pins.
# To take an urgent patch that is younger than this, use:
#   npm install <pkg>@<version> --min-release-age=0
min-release-age=7
